# SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
# Notifications: swipe to dismiss, a 25% touch close box with a vertical
# separator, and a 15 s timeout for critical notifications on touch screens.
# On a touch screen a tap runs the toast's default action and there is no right
# button; a sideways swipe moves the card with the finger and dismisses past
# 25% of its width, while the right 25% of the toast body (separated by a
# hairline above any action/reply row) is an always-enabled close box with a
# centered X. Mouse/trackpad/stylus hover (via HoverHandler) expands and pauses
# the deck without letting touch-synthesized pointer hover freeze timeouts, and
# critical notifications expire after 15 s instead of pinning permanently.
#
# Against Omarchy 4.0.6 (edge 4.0.6-1) with 0015 (inline reply) applied.
#
# Omarchy 4.5: Use the Toast scene's independent horizontal translation, a right
# 25% touch close box with a divider above deeds/reply, 15 s critical timeouts
# (including restored rows), and non-touch HoverHandler gating.

